= August 2024 — The letter from ZUS contains a larger choice

President **[+ president_name +]** has signed the widow's-pension law. Eligible
people will be able to retain part of a deceased spouse's pension instead of
losing one entitlement entirely. ZUS advisers now face the practical questions
of older claimants deciding which combination protects the household.

Włodzimierz Czarzasty spent years presenting the reform as a recognisable Left
demand. The signature turns that history into a contest over who helps people
claim it and who receives credit for enactment.
[? if left_in_government: The Left must choose between building a direct
relationship with recipients and presenting the reform as a shared coalition
achievement.?]
[? if not left_in_government: The cabinet owns enactment. Lewica can organise
claimants around its prior pressure or acknowledge the governing parties'
delivery; it cannot claim to have implemented the benefit.?]

- @widow_claim
- @widow_coalition

@widow_claim
title: [? if left_in_government: Build a claimant network around the Left's delivery?][? if not left_in_government: Organise claimants and document Lewica's prior pressure?]
subtitle: Put advice desks and Czarzasty's campaign history beside the benefit; KO will resist a shared law becoming one party's property.
on-arrival: {!
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.3;
Q.ko_relation -= 1;
Q.news_headline = Q.left_in_government
    ? "Recipients, unions and local offices put a Left name on the benefit"
    : "Lewica organises claimants without claiming cabinet implementation";
!}

Local offices open advice hours with pensioner organisations and unions. They
help claimants compare the available combinations and record where ZUS guidance
does not match the promise.

[? if left_in_government: Recipients encounter the reform through a Left-branded
network and the party gains a direct relationship to its own delivery.?][? if
not left_in_government: We document the pressure which preceded enactment
without telling claimants that opposition administered it.?] KO objects that a
coalition law is being turned into Czarzasty's receipt.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the claimant network on the events desk

@widow_coalition
title: Share credit and bank goodwill for the next social bill
subtitle: Let coalition parties and the President own enactment together; trade a distinct Lewica signature for room on the next social bill.
on-arrival: ko_relation += 3 if ministry_ko_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "ko"; psl_relation += 4 if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl"; government_coalition_dissent -= 3 if left_in_government = 1; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The coalition treats the widow's pension as proof of joint government"

The launch puts coalition partners, pensioner organisations and ZUS guidance
on one platform. No party asks a bereaved claimant to sort the parliamentary
history before applying.

Lewica receives less exclusive credit and more willingness from the parties
that actually share the cabinet to open the next social negotiation. [? if
ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": PSL remains outside
that exchange; it can support the next bill, not claim this cabinet's joint
delivery.?] The benefit becomes evidence that the government can act together
rather than evidence that only we made it act.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the shared achievement to the events desk

@movement_reckoning_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Lempart, Kotula and autonomous organisers now translate the hidden leverage calculation into a relationship, with retained consequences for services, deadlines, candidacies and party capture.
title: The abortion-rights movement audits the July outcome
subtitle: Passage, presidential action and practical access are separate tests
face-image: img/poland/events/womens-strike-2020.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 19
order: 11
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 8 and movement_reckoning_2024_done = 0 and government_party != "pis" and abortion_reform_settled = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.movement_reckoning_2024_done = 1;
let movementLeverage =
    (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 0) * 0.34 +
    (Number(Q.feminist_trust) || 0) * 0.30 +
    (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) * 0.16 +
    (Number(Q.organiser_energy) || 0) * 0.12;
if (Q.movement_origin_strategy == "Autonomous legal and safety network") {
    movementLeverage += 10;
}
if (Q.movement_origin_strategy == "Party-led mobilisation") {
    movementLeverage -= 8;
}
if (Q.abortion_strategy == "Free vote with constituency pressure") {
    movementLeverage += 5;
}
if (Q.coalition_break_threat) {
    movementLeverage += 4;
}
Q.movement_leverage = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(100, Math.round(movementLeverage))
);
Q.movement_reckoning_status = Q.abortion_law_enacted
    ? "A signed law whose practical access must be enforced"
    : (Q.abortion_presidential_action == "Presidential veto"
        ? "A parliamentary victory stopped by presidential veto"
        : (Q.abortion_presidential_action ==
                "Referred to the Constitutional Tribunal"
            ? "A parliamentary victory frozen by constitutional referral"
            : "A bill defeated in the Sejm"));
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 8;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += -4;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_left_ownership += -6;
Q.news_headline = Q.abortion_law_enacted
    ? "Organisers demand evidence that the signed law works"
    : "Organisers demand a route beyond the blocked abortion bill";
!}

= August 2024 — Political support does not mean party control

Marta Lempart and the organisers of the All-Poland Women's Strike have read the
full July chain beside Lewica MP Katarzyna Kotula. Its status is **[+
movement_reckoning_status +]**. They remember the Tribunal ruling, the deaths
in hospitals, the marches and every promise to turn support into access.

[? if movement_leverage >= 65: They arrive as an autonomous force with local
organisers, public trust and the ability to make refusal costly.?][? if
movement_leverage >= 38 and movement_leverage < 65: They still have a national
voice, but need party and parliamentary allies for the next institutional
step.?][? if movement_leverage < 38: Exhaustion and earlier party control have
left the movement dependent on the same leadership it is meant to audit.?]

In 2020 the Left built **[+ movement_origin_strategy +]**. In April it chose
**[+ abortion_strategy +]**. Those histories decide whether ministers are
hearing from autonomous partners, disappointed campaign auxiliaries or a
network the party once told to go home.

The movement asks for something enforceable: practical access now, a lawful
route past the remaining veto point, political power of its own, or an honest
admission that the party intends to absorb the campaign.

- @movement_clinical
- @movement_deadline
- @movement_candidates
- @movement_capture

@movement_clinical
title: Fund clinical guidance, legal defence and public provision now
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity in government, otherwise 1 resource. Give patients and clinicians an operating network before asking for another march.
choose-if: (left_in_government = 1 and budget >= 1) or (left_in_government = 0 and resources >= 1)
unavailable-subtitle: No implementation reserve is available.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.budget -= 1;
    Q.health_capacity += 5;
} else {
    Q.resources -= 1;
}
Q.movement_reckoning_result =
    "Clinical access and legal defence before another vote";
Q.feminist_trust += 5;
Q.movement_autonomy += 3;
if (Q.left_in_government) Q.government_delivery += 3;
else Q.local_network += 2;
Q.psl_relation -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.left_in_government
        ? (Q.abortion_law_enacted
            ? "The signed law receives an operating access network"
            : "The blocked bill still produces a legal-access network")
        : "Opposition funds legal defence and referral support, not a state programme";
!}

[? if left_in_government and abortion_law_enacted: Clinics receive guidance,
legal defence and public capacity under the signed law. Organisers can test
access against an operating service rather than a minister's promise.?][? if
left_in_government and not abortion_law_enacted: The blocked bill cannot be
implemented, but the ministry funds lawful clinical guidance and defence within
the rules that remain.?][? if not left_in_government: Lewica finances legal aid
and referral support through movement and local networks. The cabinet still
owns public provision; we have not invented a state programme from opposition.?]

Lempart's organisers retain control of the cases they bring. Kotula gains a
partner able to report where policy fails instead of an audience asked to
applaud its announcement.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the clinical network on the events desk

@movement_deadline
title: Promise another vote by spring and make failure a cabinet red line
subtitle: A dated promise raises both movement trust and coalition risk.
view-if: abortion_law_enacted = 0
on-arrival: movement_reckoning_result = "A spring vote tied to cabinet participation"; abortion_cabinet_deadline = 1; feminist_trust += 7; progressive_credibility += 4; government_coalition_dissent += 7; psl_relation -= 8; early_election_risk += 5; party_unity += 2; news_headline = "The next abortion vote receives a date and a consequence"

The leadership writes a spring date into the coalition record and states what
failure means for cabinet participation. Organisers finally receive a promise
which can be falsified rather than another sequence without an end.

[? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl": PSL begins
preparing for the threat and every minister understands that one roll call may
reopen formation.?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party !=
"psl": PSL prepares to oppose the bill, but cannot turn the deadline into a
cabinet-formation threat.?] The deadline restores trust by making Lewica's own
offices part of the collateral.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the spring deadline on the events desk

@movement_candidates
title: Reserve winnable local and parliamentary places for organisers
subtitle: Organisational power instead of another party-owned march.
on-arrival: movement_reckoning_result = "Autonomous organisers enter candidate selection"; movement_candidates_promised = 1; movement_autonomy += 5; local_network += 4; feminist_trust += 4; barons_dissent += 6; progressives_strength += 3; news_headline = "Movement organisers gain a route into political office"

Named organisers receive places in the nomination process, resources for local
campaigns and permission to keep their movement affiliations visible. They do
not have to dissolve into New Left before contesting power.

Regional barons now face candidates they did not cultivate and cannot quietly
remove. The movement gains a route from pressure to office; the party accepts
that those officeholders may still organise against it.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the candidate guarantee on the events desk

@movement_capture
title: Fold the campaign into New Left and control the next mobilisation
subtitle: Immediate message discipline; a severe loss of movement autonomy.
on-arrival: movement_reckoning_result = "Party command of the reproductive-rights campaign"; media_capacity += 4; progressive_credibility += 3; movement_autonomy -= 12; feminist_trust -= 8; barons_dissent -= 2; party_unity += 1; news_headline = "The party gains a campaign and loses independent organisers"

New Left takes the mailing lists, visual campaign and next mobilisation date
inside party command. Spokespeople receive one line and headquarters can place
the issue beside its electoral programme on demand.

Lempart's autonomous organisers refuse to become a department and take their
relationships elsewhere. We gain a disciplined campaign bearing the movement's
language and lose many of the people who made that language credible.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the party campaign on the events desk

@pkw_funding_2024
# prose-audit: Grade C — The subsidy decision, its arithmetic and the three responses are clear; the electoral commission's own members are not yet characters in it.
title: The electoral commission cuts a party's public funding
subtitle: State resources used in a campaign become a party-finance penalty
face-image: img/poland/events/election-2023-ballot.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 25
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 8 and pkw_funding_2024_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pkw_funding_2024_done = 1;
Q.pis_finance_pressure =
    (Number(Q.pis_finance_pressure) || 0) + 30;
Q.party_finance_scandal =
    (Number(Q.party_finance_scandal) || 0) + 15;
Q.institutional_issue_salience =
    (Number(Q.institutional_issue_salience) || 0) + 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "The electoral commission rejects PiS's campaign accounts and cuts its subsidy";
!}

= August 2024 — A subsidy is not an entitlement

The State Electoral Commission rejects the governing-then-opposition party's
2023 campaign financial report. Ministries, state companies and public media
spent public money on what the commission finds was campaign activity, and the
statutory consequence is a reduction of the party's public subsidy and
campaign reimbursement running to tens of millions of złoty.

Public party funding exists so that parties do not have to be bought. A
commission cutting it is therefore doing exactly what it was built to do — and
doing it to the largest opposition party, in a state where half the political
class disputes which institutions are legitimate.

[? if left_in_government = 1: Our coalition benefits directly and will be
accused, credibly enough for its own voters, of having arranged it.?][? if
left_in_government = 0: We benefit from nothing here except the precedent, and
the precedent applies to us as well.?]

[? if referendum_2023_stance = "Campaign-finance challenge": The file the
commission is ruling on is, in part, the one our lawyers opened in September
2023 while everybody else was arguing about whether to take the second
ballot.?]
[? if referendum_2023_stance = "Audit chamber referral": The audit chamber's
finding on the referendum's public spending is cited in the commission's
reasoning, which makes the 2023 referral the most productive paperwork this
party has ever filed.?]
[? if party_finance_scandal >= 20: We have already put campaign-finance
material on the record this cycle, which makes our position consistent and our
motives easier to attribute.?]

- @pkw_funding_standard
- @pkw_funding_press
- @pkw_funding_restraint
- @pkw_funding_origin

@pkw_funding_standard
title: Defend the commission's authority and apply the same standard to ourselves
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Publishes our own campaign accounts to the same test; institutionally durable, immediately expensive.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot fund an audit of its own campaign accounts this month.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; institutional_trust += 6; public_trust += 4; constitutional_restraint += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 2; nik_independence += 3; pis_relation -= 3; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The Left publishes its own campaign accounts against the same standard"

We say the unpopular thing: the commission is right, the rule is right, and
here are our own accounts measured against it. Two items in ours do not
survive contact with the standard and we correct them before anyone asks.

It costs money and a week of internal argument. It also means that when the
subsidy decision is attacked as political, the party defending it is not one
that exempted itself.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish our accounts

@pkw_funding_press
title: Press for the maximum penalty and campaign on the finding
subtitle: Converts an institutional decision into a partisan weapon and invites the same treatment when the majority changes.
on-arrival: pis_finance_pressure += 12; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; pis_relation -= 9; institutional_trust -= 4; constitutional_restraint -= 4; public_trust += 1; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The subsidy cut is campaigned on as a verdict rather than an audit"

The finding is turned into a slogan: the party that governed for eight years
was found to have run its campaign on the state's money. It is accurate, it is
satisfying, and it moves the numbers.

It also establishes that a commission decision is a political trophy. The next
majority will treat the commission accordingly, and will be able to quote us
while doing it.

- @poland_event_queue: Campaign on the finding

@pkw_funding_restraint
title: Say nothing beyond the legal text and refuse to campaign on it
subtitle: Protects the commission from becoming a partisan object; surrenders an obvious advantage for an invisible one.
on-arrival: institutional_trust += 5; constitutional_restraint += 6; public_trust += 2; left_poll_momentum -= 0.1; pis_relation += 3; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "The Left declines to campaign on the electoral commission's decision"

Our statement is four sentences of statute and no adjectives. Journalists find
it useless, which is the intention: the commission's decision has to survive
appeal, and every political sentence attached to it becomes a defence
argument.

We give up a week of easy coverage. In exchange, the institution that will one
day examine our own accounts has not been publicly adopted by us.

- @poland_event_queue: Issue the four sentences

@pkw_funding_origin
title: Publish the 2023 file that produced this decision
subtitle: Requires having opened the campaign-finance file in 2023. Establishes that the rule was enforced by evidence rather than by a change of government.
choose-if: referendum_2023_stance = "Campaign-finance challenge" or referendum_2023_stance = "Audit chamber referral"
unavailable-subtitle: We opened no finance or audit file in 2023 — there is no earlier paperwork of ours to put beside the commission's decision.
on-arrival: party_finance_scandal += 8; pis_finance_pressure += 8; institutional_trust += 7; constitutional_restraint += 5; electoral_confidence += 6; public_trust += 4; media_capacity += 3; pis_relation -= 4; news_headline = "The finance decision is traced back to a file opened before the election"

We publish the September 2023 submission with its date stamp. The commission
did not act because the government changed; it acted on material lodged while
the accused party was still in office and still expected to win.

That distinction is the whole argument about whether this is enforcement or
revenge, and it is one of the very few in Polish politics that can be settled
by showing somebody a piece of paper.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the original file
